From: Robin Kertels
Subject: [d3d9] Ignore zero extent stretch rect (backport to v2.7.1)
Origin: https://github.com/doitsujin/dxvk/commit/d2762330fbc0d7921ed30a7f5069eca60f79456b

Mirrors Edge does a call with src rect 0,0,0,0
and dst rect 0,0,0,0.

The upstream change is preserved; only the hunk line number is adjusted
for v2.7.1. This is an Aura backport, not an upstream release artifact.
License: zlib/libpng; see LICENSE.dxvk.

--- a/src/d3d9/d3d9_device.cpp
+++ b/src/d3d9/d3d9_device.cpp
@@ -1326,6 +1326,10 @@
       uint32_t(blitInfo.dstOffsets[1].y - blitInfo.dstOffsets[0].y),
       uint32_t(blitInfo.dstOffsets[1].z - blitInfo.dstOffsets[0].z) };
 
+    if (unlikely(srcCopyExtent.width == 0 || srcCopyExtent.height == 0
+      || dstCopyExtent.width == 0 || dstCopyExtent.height == 0))
+      return D3D_OK;
+
     bool srcIsDS = IsDepthStencilFormat(srcFormat);
     bool dstIsDS = IsDepthStencilFormat(dstFormat);
     if (unlikely(srcIsDS || dstIsDS)) {
